.1\",\nstats/org.apache.curator/curator-client/5.0.0/execution-metrics.json:86:      \"library\": \"org.apache.curator:curator-client:5.0.0\",\nstats/org.apache.curator/curator-client/5.0.0/execution-metrics.json:87:      \"summary\": \"The javac errors come from the 2.7.1 test source using APIs that curator-client 5.0.0 no longer has: the `org.apache.curator.ensemble.exhibitor` package, and the static `RetryLoop.shouldRetry` and `isRetryException` methods. This is a test-code API incompatibility that the repair step can fix by adapting the tests to the 5.0.0 API. I did not inspect the repository or the 5.0.0 artifact, so the cause rests on the issue's compile errors alone. Nothing in the failure points to a missing dependency, Docker image or system property, and no Native Image-unsupported mechanism is involved.\",\nstats/org.apache.curator/curator-client/5.0.0/execution-metrics.json:89:      \"agent_guidance\": \"Port the 2.7.1 tests to the 5.0.0 API instead of copying them. Drop the Exhibitor ensemble-provider tests (`ExhibitorEnsembleProvider`, `Exhibitors`, `ExhibitorRestClient`, `DefaultExhibitorRestClient`), because that package is absent from the 5.0.0 artifact. Replace the removed static `RetryLoop.shouldRetry` and `RetryLoop.isRetryException` calls with whatever 5.0.0 exposes, for example `RetryLoop.getDefaultRetrySleeper()` or `RetryLoop.callWithRetry`. Reach retry-policy behavior through public classes such as `RetryNTimes` and `ExponentialBackoffRetry`. Check the 5.0.0 jar for the actual public API before writing code. Keep the existing ZooKeeper dependency in `build.gradle`, bumped to a version compatible with curator-client 5.0.0 (ZooKeeper 3.6.x line) if the build does not already resolve it transitively.\",\nstats/org.apache.curator/curator-client/5.0.0/execution-metrics.json:93:        \"curator-client 5.0.0 pulls in ZooKeeper 3.6.x, which may add transitive dependencies or require reflection metadata not present for 2.7.1.\"\nstats/org.apache.cur